<Track #add-provider-epoch-and-deepseek-conversation-projection apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" version="1" { status = "completed" goal = "Make provider switching across recovered tool-rich conversations protocol-correct, observable and recoverable through a single canonical conversation authority plus durable provider epochs." description = "Repair the incident where a recovered Codex conversation cannot continue on SiliconFlow DeepSeek by adding closed wire projection, safe admission diagnostics, explicit compatibility profiles and context-epoch handoff semantics." question_mode = "decision-tree" question_severity = "auto" commit_mode = "manual" created_at = "2026-08-24T18:08:11.656Z" updated_at = "2026-08-24T19:44:27.391Z" modeling_base_commit = "94436d0e142762fdadeb6fad22502bfdaca6956b" engineering_base_commit = "94436d0e142762fdadeb6fad22502bfdaca6956b" } (
  <Ports { scope = "track" } [
    <MaterialBundle #behavior_deltas { role = "input" name = "behavior-deltas" domain = "behavior" path = "vfs://./behavior_deltas/" }>
  ]>
  <TaskSpace #space_add-provider-epoch-and-deepseek-conversation-projection { name = "add-provider-epoch-and-deepseek-conversation-projection" version = "1" } (
    <SubNodes [
      <TaskGroup #P1 { name = "Closed DeepSeek request projection and diagnostics" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 0 } (
        <Description ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKM9>
        First reproduce the exact local admission failure, then make Chat/DeepSeek wire projection closed and diagnostics safe without changing canonical history.
        </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKM9>
        <Gate [
          <Criterion { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMA>
          The incident-shaped request is either admitted or rejected with a safe exact structural diagnostic before network send.
          </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMA>
          <Criterion { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMB>
          DeepSeek wire body contains only profile-approved provider fields.
          </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMB>
        ]>
        <SubNodes [
          <Task #P1-T1 { name = "Establish provider request RED and incident diagnostic" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 0 } (
            <Description ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMC>
            Add focused tests for non-own-data message fields, SiliconFlow DeepSeek request shape and the copied incident session, proving the current generic invalid_provider_request_body failure.
            </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMC>
            <Acceptance [
              <Criterion #P1-T1-AC1 { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMD>
              A failing test captures the exact safe path/kind without exposing values.
              </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMD>
              <Criterion #P1-T1-AC2 { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKME>
              A failing test proves runtime-only capability/cache metadata is currently present on DeepSeek wire requests.
              </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKME>
              <Criterion #P1-T1-AC3 { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMF>
              The original accident session is never mutated by the harness.
              </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMF>
              <Criterion #P1-T1-AC4 { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMG>
              Official and compatible profile selection is driven by an explicit versioned config field; unknown values and heuristic selection fail closed.
              </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMG>
            ]>
          )>
          <Task #P1-T2 { name = "Implement closed Chat projection and safe admission" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 1 } (
            <Description ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMH>
            Rebuild role-specific wire messages from allow-listed own-data, add safe typed admission diagnostics and keep capability/cache facts outside the provider body.
            </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMH>
            <Acceptance [
              <Criterion #P1-T2-AC1 { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMJ>
              Unknown/internal/undefined/accessor fields cannot enter admitted body.
              </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMJ>
              <Criterion #P1-T2-AC2 { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMK>
              Diagnostic fields contain no prompt, tool arguments/results, credentials or full body.
              </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMK>
              <Criterion #P1-T2-AC3 { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMM>
              OpenAI Chat isolation and DeepSeek native reasoning roundtrip regressions remain green.
              </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMM>
            ]>
          )>
        ]>
      )>
      <TaskGroup #P2 { name = "Provider epoch and recoverable model switching" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 1 } (
        <Description ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMN>
        Make cross-provider switching advance the existing conversation context epoch and use a provider-neutral handoff instead of replaying incompatible tool protocol.
        </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMN>
        <Gate [
          <Criterion { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMP>
          Provider switch and fresh recovery use one durable epoch receipt bound to the canonical source frontier.
          </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMP>
          <Criterion { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMQ>
          Projection failure leaves the interactive session continuable and does not repeat tool effects.
          </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMQ>
        ]>
        <SubNodes [
          <Task #P2-T1 { name = "Establish provider epoch and recovery RED" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 0 } (
            <Description ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMR>
            Add tests for Codex tool history to DeepSeek handoff, DeepSeek native reasoning recovery, model switch epoch advance and post-admission failure continuation.
            </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMR>
            <Acceptance [
              <Criterion #P2-T1-AC1 { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMS>
              Cross-profile switch test rejects raw incompatible tool replay and fabricated reasoning.
              </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMS>
              <Criterion #P2-T1-AC2 { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMT>
              Fresh recovery test requires stable epoch/frontier receipt and one tool effect.
              </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMT>
              <Criterion #P2-T1-AC3 { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMV>
              Interactive failure test requires fiber to return to a recoverable suspended state.
              </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMV>
              <Criterion #P2-T1-AC4 { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMW>
              Pending, delivered, legacy-no-delivery-fact and handoff failure/recovery cases preserve first-delivery authority without duplicate tool execution.
              </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMW>
            ]>
          )>
          <Task #P2-T2 { name = "Implement provider epoch handoff and retry semantics" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 1 } (
            <Description ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMX>
            Reuse Conversation Domain contextEpoch and continuation reset, persist a closed provider projection receipt, and make local projection failure retryable without a second history owner.
            </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMX>
            <Acceptance [
              <Criterion #P2-T2-AC1 { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMY>
              Provider/profile changes advance epoch exactly once and same-profile retry does not.
              </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMY>
              <Criterion #P2-T2-AC2 { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMZ>
              Handoff is bounded, role-ordered, digest-bound and contains no provider-native tool framing.
              </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKMZ>
              <Criterion #P2-T2-AC3 { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKN0>
              Canonical History and ToolCallDomain bytes/facts remain unchanged by projection.
              </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKN0>
              <Criterion #P2-T2-AC4 { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKN1>
              Receipt identity, Conversation Domain owner slot, atomic switch order, corruption fallback and duplicate control idempotence are implemented and fresh-recovery tested.
              </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKN1>
            ]>
          )>
        ]>
      )>
      <TaskGroup #P3 { name = "Incident replay and bounded verification" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 2 } (
        <Description ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKN2>
        Build the current terminal, validate the copied session with SiliconFlow DeepSeek, and run bounded provider/session regressions.
        </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKN2>
        <Gate [
          <Criterion { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKN3>
          The copied incident session completes a DeepSeek turn or reaches a typed remote provider failure, never local invalid_provider_request_body.
          </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKN3>
          <Criterion { checked = true } ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKN4>
          Focused tests, terminal build, strict Codument validation and diff checks pass.
          </?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKN4>
        ]>
        <SubNodes [
          <Task #P3-T1 { name = "Verify copied incident and regression matrix" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 0 } (
            <Description ?01M0TGE93V45FY1DJVXKMAGKN5>
